## 7️⃣ Generating / Converting a PMTiles file (quick recap)

| Tool | Input → Output | One‑liner |
|------|----------------|-----------|
| **tippecanoe** (v2.17+) | GeoJSON → PMTiles | `tippecanoe -zg -o mydata.pmtiles data.geojson` |
| **tippecanoe** (older) | GeoJSON → MBTiles → PMTiles | `tippecanoe -o mydata.mbtiles data.geojson && pmtiles convert mydata.mbtiles mydata.pmtiles` |
| **Planetiler** | OSM PBF → PMTiles | `java -jar planetiler.jar --area=monaco --output=monaco.pmtiles` |
| **GDAL (≥3.8)** | Shapefile/PostGIS → PMTiles | `ogr2ogr -f PMTiles out.pmtiles input.shp` |
| **pmtiles CLI** | MBTiles → PMTiles | `pmtiles convert in.mbtiles out.pmtiles` |
| **pmtiles CLI** | Inspect | `pmtiles show out.pmtiles` |
| **pmtiles CLI** | Extract a region/zoom subset | `pmtiles extract --bbox=-10,35,10,45 --minzoom=5 --maxzoom=12 out.pmtiles subregion.pmtiles` |

Once you have the `.pmtiles` file, upload it to your static host, set the CORS & cache headers, and you’re ready to load it as shown above.

